[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-277
TITLE: Get Interlocks state
STATEMENT: >>>
The interlock dialog view model derives ``SystemIsReady`` from the latest immutable
telemetry snapshot, the attached applicator, the registered applicator collection, and the
treatment-plan applicator configuration. Readiness requires a clear buffered master-fault
input, no active system fault, every required interlock to be available and active, and a
ready applicator check.

The view model publishes four operator-facing groups: E-stops, Door closed, Keys, and one
Applicator row. It first treats a missing attached applicator as ``No applicator``; then an
attached serial absent from the registered collection as ``Unknown applicator``; then a
registered applicator whose configuration differs from the treatment plan as ``Incorrect
applicator``. Otherwise the row is ``Applicator`` with the existing green thumbs-up state.
This ordered evaluation is shared by both interlock view models, so any error makes
``SystemIsReady`` false and exactly one applicator row is displayed.

E-stop and key groups aggregate their base and remote inputs and disclose their
individual child rows only while the group is not ready or is unavailable.

Other physical inputs are aggregated into operator-facing subsystem names. The Auxiliary
safety circuit group contains spare interlocks 1 and 2. Only groups with a false state
enter the attention collection. The buffered master-fault state enters that collection
as Master fault only when it is false and every other available interlock is ready.
Unavailable technical signals are not reported as bad.

``FaultsChangedEvent`` snapshots rebuild one false-state attention row per active
``FaultEntry.Message``. The inherited ``ForegroundDefaultBrush`` on the pop-up root keeps
body and row text consistent with the prior gray interlock-dialog styling while section
headings retain ``AccentForegroundColor``. ``ShowClearFaultsButton`` additionally checks
``IHeraclesExternalSettings`` and becomes true when the buffered master-fault input is bad,
the telemetry fault mask is nonzero, or the active fault list is nonempty. The fixed
bottom Clear Errors button reuses the existing refresh-plus-cancel icon treatment, invokes
``IMainBoardAPI.ClearFaults``, and reports command failures through
``IPopUpService``. The same button remains collapsed in the Internal GUI.

.. raw:: html

    <pre class="mermaid">
    sequenceDiagram
        participant InterlocksDialog
        participant InterlocksDialogViewModel
        participant GCBDataStore
        participant SystemInterlocks
        participant MainBoardAPI

        GCBDataStore-->>InterlocksDialogViewModel: SystemTelemetryChangedEvent
        GCBDataStore-->>InterlocksDialogViewModel: FaultsChangedEvent
        InterlocksDialogViewModel->>SystemInterlocks: derive readiness and grouped states
        SystemInterlocks-->>InterlocksDialogViewModel: tri-state semantic values
        InterlocksDialogViewModel-->>InterlocksDialog: readiness, operator checks, bad groups, fault messages, clear visibility
        InterlocksDialog-->>InterlocksDialog: disclose failed e-stop and key children
        InterlocksDialog->>InterlocksDialogViewModel: ClearFaultsCommand [External GUI only]
        InterlocksDialogViewModel->>MainBoardAPI: ClearFaults
    </pre>
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-139
  ROLE: Refines

