[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-272
TITLE: LogService module
STATEMENT: >>>
The action audit service records explicit preparation, Beam On, and Stop commands with the acting user and treatment identifiers. Delivery outcome records use measured emission results and distinguish completed, cancelled, and failed delivery from the requested emission. Background telemetry, automatic refreshes, and low-level RPC activity do not create user-action records.

.. image:: _images/SW-H10TG-272.png
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-89
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-259
TITLE: Perform Quality Checks
STATEMENT: >>>
The external application routes QC-board ping and acquisition commands through
``GcbCommandInterface`` and main control. The start request is exactly ``[1, 0]`` and must return
Armed before Beam On is sent. The stop request is exactly ``[2, 0]``. Stop polls Starting,
Accumulating, or Stopping responses within one shared two-second deadline; Complete returns the
unsigned channel 0 sum, channel 1 sum, channel 0 sample count, channel 1 sample count, and numeric
session status. Error or deadline expiry fails the acquisition.

``QcReadings`` retains its immutable two-channel wire result. Channel 0 carries the single analog
diode acquisition; channel 1 remains present for compatibility and is zero and disconnected.
Reports persist exactly the two accumulation values while retaining each channel's independent
sample count as metadata. Normal GCB telemetry exposes both wire channels' accumulations,
instantaneous readings, and ADC connection states. UCSI identifies all QC values in counts, records
schema version 2 with the two accumulation columns, and reads schema version 1 recordings with
those fields represented as null.

The flow for performing Daily Quality Checks is:

.. raw:: html

   <pre class="mermaid">
   sequenceDiagram
       autonumber
       actor User

       box Application
           participant QualityCheckViewModel
           participant MainBoardModel
           participant GcbQcbService
           participant GcbCommandInterface
           participant QcReportService
       end
       box Control system
           participant MainControl
           participant QcDetector
       end

       Note over QualityCheckViewModel: build the list of calibrated QA emissions
       User->>QualityCheckViewModel: select energy and exactly one emission

       User->>QualityCheckViewModel: Prepare
       activate QualityCheckViewModel
       QualityCheckViewModel->>GcbQcbService: PingBoardAsync
       GcbQcbService->>GcbCommandInterface: PingQcb
       GcbCommandInterface->>MainControl: [UDP] QC-board ping
       MainControl->>QcDetector: check connection
       QcDetector-->>MainControl: connection status
       MainControl-->>GcbCommandInterface: validated ping response
       GcbCommandInterface-->>GcbQcbService: connection status
       GcbQcbService-->>QualityCheckViewModel: connection status
       alt detector is unavailable
           QualityCheckViewModel-->>User: return to StandBy and display preparation error
       else detector is available
           QualityCheckViewModel->>MainBoardModel: load selected emission
           MainBoardModel-->>QualityCheckViewModel: selected emission confirmed
           QualityCheckViewModel-->>User: enable Beam On
       end
       deactivate QualityCheckViewModel

       User->>QualityCheckViewModel: Beam On
       activate QualityCheckViewModel
       QualityCheckViewModel->>GcbQcbService: start detector acquisition
       GcbQcbService->>GcbCommandInterface: StartQcbReadings
       GcbCommandInterface->>MainControl: [UDP] [Start, 0]
       MainControl->>QcDetector: command Accumulating and wait for Active
       QcDetector-->>MainControl: Active
       MainControl-->>GcbCommandInterface: Armed
       GcbCommandInterface-->>GcbQcbService: start accepted
       GcbQcbService-->>QualityCheckViewModel: start accepted
       QualityCheckViewModel->>MainBoardModel: Beam On selected emission
       MainBoardModel-->>QualityCheckViewModel: emission entered
       QualityCheckViewModel->>GcbQcbService: stop readings
       GcbQcbService->>GcbCommandInterface: StopQcbReadings
       loop shared two-second deadline
           GcbCommandInterface->>MainControl: [UDP] [Stop, 0]
           MainControl-->>GcbCommandInterface: sums, counts, session status
       end
       GcbCommandInterface-->>GcbQcbService: immutable two-channel QcReadings
       GcbQcbService-->>QualityCheckViewModel: selected-emission readings
       alt acquisition failed or timed out
           QualityCheckViewModel->>GcbQcbService: one best-effort Stop
           QualityCheckViewModel->>MainBoardModel: Stop
           QualityCheckViewModel-->>User: display acquisition error
       else acquisition completed
           MainBoardModel-->>QualityCheckViewModel: selected emission completed
           QualityCheckViewModel->>MainBoardModel: reset timers and clear plan
           QualityCheckViewModel->>QcReportService: save selected emission and two channel sums
           QcReportService-->>QualityCheckViewModel: report saved
           Note over QualityCheckViewModel: return to StandBy and clear selection
           QualityCheckViewModel-->>User: selected emission completed
       end
       deactivate QualityCheckViewModel
   </pre>
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-66
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-280
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-282
TITLE: Authoritative Physics Configuration Synchronization
STATEMENT: >>>
``CollimatorService`` first fetches the active head, the complete collimator-configuration list, and the collimators. It then calls ``CollimatorModel.Reset`` once with all three results. Reset links each collimator to the configuration identified by its foreign key, replaces both observable collections, and raises the configuration-change notification only after the complete snapshot is available. Consumers therefore do not observe a partially rebuilt configuration list.

The database list services enforce the request's parent identifier when reading the hierarchy: presets are filtered by collimator-configuration identifier; coils, correction matrices, heater-current configurations, output factors, and reference fields are filtered by preset identifier; and an optional collimator-configuration identifier filters collimators. Rows belonging to another parent are never returned as part of the requested configuration.

The Physics view responds to the complete configuration-change notification by rebuilding its selectable applicator and energy options and forcing a refresh of their physics data. Refreshes are serialized. A successful refresh replaces the physics-data store so entries absent from the authoritative snapshot are removed. A failed configuration read is logged with its identifier, type, and energy; when every requested configuration fails, the refresh reports an error and remains retryable.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-280
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-260
TITLE: Perform System Safety Checks
STATEMENT: >>>
The flow for performing System Safety Checks should be implemented as described in the following sequence diagram:

.. raw:: html

   <pre class="mermaid">
   sequenceDiagram
       autonumber
       actor User
       
       box Application
           participant SafetyCheckViewModel
           participant SafetyCheckModel
           participant MainBoardModel
       end
       box Database
           participant SafetyCheckService
       end

       SafetyCheckViewModel->>SafetyCheckModel: fetch SafetyCheck reports
       activate SafetyCheckViewModel
       activate SafetyCheckModel
       SafetyCheckModel->>SafetyCheckService: grpc: read report list
       activate SafetyCheckService
       SafetyCheckService-->>SafetyCheckModel: grpc: stored reports
       deactivate SafetyCheckService
       SafetyCheckModel-->>SafetyCheckViewModel: 
       deactivate SafetyCheckModel

       alt "[SafetyCheck is allowed with current collimator type]"
           Note over SafetyCheckViewModel: prepare one scalar SafetyCheck emission
           SafetyCheckViewModel->>SafetyCheckViewModel: 
           Note over SafetyCheckViewModel: enable Prepare button
           
           User->>SafetyCheckViewModel: Prepare
           SafetyCheckViewModel->>MainBoardModel: load scalar emission
           activate MainBoardModel
           
           Note over MainBoardModel: send scalar point and confirmation to ControlBoard
           MainBoardModel->>MainBoardModel: 
           Note over MainBoardModel: wait for Ready state
           MainBoardModel->>MainBoardModel: 
           
           MainBoardModel-->>SafetyCheckViewModel: task status
           deactivate MainBoardModel
           Note over SafetyCheckViewModel: enable BeamOn button
           
           loop "[User starts/stops/resumes emission]"
               Note over SafetyCheckViewModel: make checks one by one
               SafetyCheckViewModel->>SafetyCheckViewModel: 
               Note over SafetyCheckViewModel: toggle check UI controls
           end
           
           User->>SafetyCheckViewModel: save SafetyCheck report
           SafetyCheckViewModel->>SafetyCheckModel: add new record
           activate SafetyCheckModel
           
           SafetyCheckModel->>SafetyCheckService: create new record
           activate SafetyCheckService
           SafetyCheckService-->>SafetyCheckModel: stored record
           deactivate SafetyCheckService
           
           Note over SafetyCheckModel: add record to the list
           SafetyCheckModel->>SafetyCheckModel: 
           SafetyCheckModel-->>SafetyCheckViewModel: 
           deactivate SafetyCheckModel
           
           SafetyCheckViewModel->>MainBoardModel: clear plan
           activate MainBoardModel
           Note over MainBoardModel: send ResetTimers/ClearPlan commands to ControlBoard
           MainBoardModel->>MainBoardModel: 
           MainBoardModel-->>SafetyCheckViewModel: task status
           deactivate MainBoardModel
           
           Note over SafetyCheckViewModel: navigate to SafetyCheck reports view
           SafetyCheckViewModel->>SafetyCheckViewModel: 
           SafetyCheckViewModel-->>User: 
       end
       deactivate SafetyCheckViewModel
   </pre>
<<<
