[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-281
TITLE: QC Result Persistence, Acceptance, and Approval
STATEMENT: >>>
``QcReportService`` creates one ``QcSampleHeader`` per collimator configuration with the
current creation time and the authorized operator's email address. ``QcRepository`` persists
that header, its QA-emission fields, and each field's diode intensities as a parent-child
hierarchy. The SQLite gRPC repositories preserve the creation timestamps and parent identifiers
and filter samples by collimator configuration, fields by sample, and intensities by field.
When opening an existing table, the repository backfills an empty indexed parent identifier
from the serialized record before serving the filtered reads.

``QcTreatmentAcceptanceService`` orders the selected configuration's samples by creation time
and identifier, uses the newest sample and newest referenced sample, and returns:

* ``Missing`` when the newest sample does not exist or is older than 24 hours;
* ``Accepted`` immediately when the newest sample has a persisted approver;
* ``NoReference`` when an unapproved current sample has no reference;
* otherwise, ``Accepted`` only when the two samples have the same non-empty ordered field and
  value shape and every value's absolute deviation is less than 3 percent; all other cases
  return ``Failed``.

Deviation calculation returns zero for a zero value against a zero reference. A nonzero value
against zero, a null value, a missing field, or a mismatched value count cannot pass acceptance.

``QCSampleService`` authenticates an approval request against the persisted users before
loading or updating the sample. Username matching is case-insensitive and the supplied password
must match and the persisted failed-login count must be below 10. Authentication failure returns
``Unauthenticated`` without modifying the sample; success stores the authenticated user's email
address in ``ApprovedBy``. These approval checks neither increment nor reset the failed-login count.
<<<
