[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-248
TITLE: Treatment Staging Sequence
STATEMENT: >>>

.. raw:: html

    <pre class="mermaid">
    sequenceDiagram
        box Application
            participant M as MainBoardModel
        end
        box ControlBoard
            participant F as Firmware
        end

        Note over M, F: Board is in Primed state, User initiates plan preparation

        M->>F: [UDP] create an argument-free scalar session
        activate F
        F-->>M: [UDP] session key
        deactivate F

        M->>M: wait for Staging board state

        M->>F: [UDP] send scalar emission parameters
        activate F
        F-->>M: [UDP] status response
        deactivate F

        M->>F: [UDP] Stage command
        activate F
        F-->>M: [UDP] status response
        deactivate F

        M->>M: wait for Staged board state
    </pre>
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-31
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-34
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-268
TITLE: Treatment View Layout
STATEMENT: >>>
The layout should include:

1. The plan's treatment fields are listed on a table.
2. A visual representation of the collimator.
3. The system telemetry: System status, Main timer (in sec), backup timers (T1 & T2) (in sec), Energy (in kV), and Current ( in mA).
4. Prepare button - which will prepare the system for the radiation (i.e., warmup and loading).
5. Beam-On - a multi-state control for triggering the emission, resetting timers, and clearing errors.
6. Stop button - Stops the emission.
7. Interlocks visualization.
8. Live Camera to monitor the patient.

.. image:: _images/SW-H10TG-268.png
<<<
