[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-256
TITLE: Warmup Progress Monitoring
STATEMENT: >>>
Warmup progress consumes immutable semantic snapshots published from unsolicited telemetry.
The warmup model uses the available heater-current setpoint to calculate and publish the
progress value.

.. raw:: html

    <pre class="mermaid">
    sequenceDiagram
        participant M as WarmupModel
        participant WP as WarmupProgress
        participant DS as GCBDataStore

        Note over M, DS: User initiates Warmup/Conditioning
        DS-->>M: SystemTelemetryChanged(immutable snapshot)
        M->>M: Read available HeaterCurrentSetpoint
        M->>M: Calculate warmup progress
        M->>WP: Notify progress value change
    </pre>
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-12
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-251
TITLE: prompt the user when an interlock triggered during emission
STATEMENT: >>>
.. raw:: html

    <pre class="mermaid">
    sequenceDiagram
        actor User
        participant VM as OperatePlanViewModelBase
        participant M as MainBoardModel
        participant D as DialogService
        participant DS as GCBDataStore
        participant F as Firmware

        User->>VM: BeamOn
        VM->>M: BeamOn
        M->>F: [UDP] ReleasePoint command
        F-->>M: [UDP] command response
        M->>M: Wait for emission termination

        F-->>DS: Unsolicited telemetry routed through processor
        DS-->>VM: SystemTelemetryChanged
        VM->>VM: Check control-board state and active faults

        alt Board is in Fault state
            VM->>M: Cancel current task
            M-->>VM: BeamOn task cancellation exception
            VM->>D: Show emission error dialog
            D-->>User: Error dialog
        end
    </pre>
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-73
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-279
TITLE: Calibration Mode Clinical Lockout
STATEMENT: >>>
The external tab view binds each clinical tab's enabled state to the immutable telemetry
firmware mode in addition to the existing plan-loaded navigation constraint. Calibration
mode disables the Treatment and Quality Assurance tabs. A high-z-order overlay inside each
tab obscures previously rendered content and displays the service-required message.
Unknown or unavailable firmware mode does not lock the tabs.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-285
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-280
TITLE: Display Main Control Firmware Version
STATEMENT: >>>
The version-information parser accepts the 19-word control-board response and decodes its
null-padded 32-byte ASCII version fields. When the user opens System Information, the
external tab view requests device information and displays the decoded main-control
``FirmwareVersion`` string.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-286
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H10TG-283
TITLE: Permission-Based Navigation Composition
STATEMENT: >>>
The external application derives the visible navigation items from the authenticated user's
permissions when composing the left navigation menu and Quality Assurance tabs. The
Treatment menu item requires treatment permission, and the Physics tab requires physics
quality-assurance permission. Items for which the user lacks permission are omitted rather
than displayed as actionable controls.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H10TG-287
  ROLE: Refines

